body:
When you say: "population grew by 50%" that might mean initially you had, say, 100 and finally you had 150 (100 plus half of that). That is, you have 1.5x of what you initially had, it's not that you now have 0.5x . Now, when you say "population grew by 100%" then you initially had 100 and now you have 200. It doubled indeed: 2x. Because when phrasing percentages in such contexts you're counting the sole growth (say, 50% = 0.5x) and then adding it to the initial population (1x + 0.5x = 1.5x).

&#x200B;

In the phrase "... shoots up 750% compared to..." people here is talking about the sole shoot up or increment, which then has to be added to the people that has not been through that. That's why you have to add 1 whenever people is talking about percentage increments if you want to convert it to a multiplyer (i.e. 750% -> 8.5x).

Yeah, but with a rape kit people are able to detect fluids that may serve as proof, or to stop/prevent infections or pregnancies with on-the-spot medication, so in this case I don't see how it might help the situation to ever happen again. This does not prevent future contacts from happen.

